<title>FINLAND: ARSENAL 1996 LOSS NARROWS, SEES SMALLER 1997 LOSS.</title>
<headline>ARSENAL 1996 LOSS NARROWS, SEES SMALLER 1997 LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31-</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Loss for the financial year		  1,352 vs 5,253</p>
<p> Credit, guarantee losses			 987 vs 3,732</p>
<p> Depreciations					209 vs 221</p>
<p> Balance sheet				   20,254 vs 23,435</p>
<p> Real estate sales				1,508 vs 1,312</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Finnish state-owned asset management</p>
<p>company is Arsenal Oy. In a statement, the company repeated</p>
<p>that it expected its 1997 loss to be clearly smaller than in</p>
<p>1996. The balance sheet would shrink to some 18 billion markka.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
